        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add CLI cards view",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add `codexbar cards`, a one-shot terminal usage snapshot with a responsive provider card grid.\n- Add `codexbar cards --brief`, a compact Provider / Usage / Reset table with account context and enhanced terminal colors.\n- Reuse the existing `codexbar usage` fetch pipeline, preserve partial successes, and summarize provider failures in a footer.\n- Keep card, table, reset, detail, warning, and account labels bounded on narrow terminals.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nSynthetic fixture data only (`example.test` identities and fixed quota values); no live account, cookie, Keychain, or provider access.\n\n### Card grid\n\n<img width=\"884\" height=\"640\" alt=\"codexbar cards synthetic provider grid\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e7e3fea-d03f-4ab7-bec0-426d866d47b2\" />\n\n### Brief view\n\n<img width=\"840\" height=\"416\" alt=\"codexbar cards brief synthetic usage table\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d429a510-156d-487c-b47a-aac913ac2a71\" />\n\n## Validation\n\n- `swift test --filter 'CLICards|CLITerminalCapabilities'` — 49 tests in 3 suites passed.\n- `make check` — SwiftFormat and strict SwiftLint clean.\n- `make test` — all 49 shards passed (578 selections).\n- `git diff --check` — clean.\n- Autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Validated head: `523dd33bc2686ce3e8fd3903c3b0861599a6ed9d`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The separate `cards` command and `CODEXBAR_CARDS_ENHANCED=1` override are intentional supported CLI surface.\n- Synthetic placeholder quota lanes are omitted, detail-backed quotas are not mislabeled as resets, and reset display style is honored.\n- `Package.swift` and `Package.resolved` remain unchanged; no dependency added.\n- User-facing changelog entry added by the maintainer, with thanks to @DonnieFi.\n",
